; Stage 15 W4d (design/stage15-stress-test/diagnostics.md §W4d): the generic
; fixed-arity mismatch message. Before this fix, every fixed-arity macro
; called with the wrong argument count died with the bare, unlocated-by-name
; `macro: wrong number of args` (naming neither the macro nor the counts).
; `for` is `(defmacro for (init test step body))` (lib/macros.nuc), a fixed
; 4-arg macro; this call passes 5. After: `macro 'for': expects 4 args, got
; 5`, located at the call's own line (line 11).
(import-use "stdio.h")

(defn main ():i32
  (for (i:i32 0) (< i 3) (inc! i) (printf "x\n") 99)
  (return 0))
